        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(message): preserve stringified channelData payloads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where message actions that pass channel-specific `channelData` as a JSON string could lose that payload or fail to treat it as send content when the visible text is blank or removed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe message tool, outbound runner, and embedded subscribe rich-content tracker now parse `channelData` with the same structured JSON boundary used for sibling message payload fields. The message-tool path also rejects opaque `channelData` that contains protected internal runtime context before dispatch, and the runner now counts valid `channelData` as real send content without adding config, schema, provider, or compatibility behavior.\n\nDuplicate search found no open or closed overlapping PRs or open issues for `channelData JSON message action`, `stringified channelData`, `message-tool channelData idempotency`, or `parseJsonMessageParam channelData`; open self PRs had no same-root outbound/message parameter normalization overlap.\n\n## User Impact\n\nChannel-native cards, buttons, and other provider payload metadata can be preserved when passed as JSON strings, including internal source replies that intentionally carry channel-specific structured data without visible text. Protected runtime context remains filtered before those opaque payloads can be sent.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: stringified `channelData` is parsed before message-tool dispatch and outbound runner validation, channelData-only sends remain dispatchable after visible text is stripped, embedded rich-content detection still recognizes channelData-only payloads, and protected internal runtime context inside opaque channelData keys or values is removed before dispatch.\n- Current head: `1dae697b50ec846f89cc7db66b750cf2901c9f60`.\n- Runtime transcript: `node --import tsx --input-type=module -` directly executed `createMessageTool` with an injected dry-run outbound sink. Observed `safeChannelDataOnlyDispatched=true`, `safeVisibleMessageAfterSanitize=\"\"`, `mixedChannelDataRemoved=true`, and `leakedBootMarker=false` for a stringified Slack-style `channelData` payload containing mixed prefix/suffix internal runtime context.\n- Focused regression proof: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/message-tool.test.ts -t \"message tool internal-runtime-context sanitization\"` passed with 40 tests and 216 skipped.\n- Targeted format: `node_modules\\.bin\\oxfmt.CMD --check --threads=1 src\\agents\\tools\\message-tool.ts src\\agents\\tools\\message-tool.test.ts` passed.\n- Diff hygiene: `git diff --check` passed before commit.\n- Review proof: `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode local --codex-bin C:\\Users\\86158\\.codex\\codex-pixel-autoreview.cmd` passed with no accepted/actionable findings.",
        "branch": "codex/fix-channeldata-json",
